---
/**
 * What players ask before they play, read the way the game has you read
 * signs along a road: each question on its own plank, its answer right under
 * it, nothing folded away. Works without JavaScript and every answer is in
 * the page for search and screen readers.
 */
import Sign from "~/components/Sign.astro"
import { PATCHER_URL, REPOSITORY_URL } from "~/lib/content"
import { RELEASE_LABEL } from "~/lib/release"
---

<section aria-labelledby="faq" class="period-night night-sky">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
    <div class="waypoint">
      <Sign>QUESTIONS</Sign>
    </div>
    <h2 id="faq" class="pixel-heading mt-5">Before you set out</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/80">
      The signs at the edge of town. Read them once and you're ready to go.
    </p>

    <dl class="faq mt-12 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">How do I play it?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>
            Wayfarer comes as a .ups patch. Apply it to your own Pokémon Emerald (U) ROM, for example
            with <a href={PATCHER_URL}>Rom Patcher JS</a> in your browser, and play the patched ROM in an
            emulator. The patch doesn't include the game itself.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">Which emulators work?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>Any up-to-date emulator that runs ROM hacks. These are known to work:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>PC and Mac:</strong> mGBA</li>
            <li><strong>Android:</strong> Pizza Boy, Lemuroid, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
            <li><strong>iOS:</strong> Delta, Ignited, or RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
            <li><strong>Linux handhelds:</strong> RetroArch with the mGBA core</li>
          </ul>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">How does it battle?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>
            With modern mechanics: the physical and special split, and updated stats, types and moves. TMs
            are reusable, so teach them as often as you like.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">Can I trade and battle with friends?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>
            Yes. Trades and battles over the GBA link work, with a link cable or your emulator's link play.
            The GameCube, e-Reader and Berry Fix extras are gone.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">Will my save carry over to updates?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>From v1.0 on, yes. Updates after that keep your save.</p>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">Is it free?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>
            Yes. Wayfarer is a free fan game, and you can follow every change{" "}
            <a href={REPOSITORY_URL}>on GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <div>
        <Sign as="dt">When does it come out?</Sign>
        <dd>
          <p>
            On {RELEASE_LABEL}. <a href="/wayfarer-release.ics" download>Add it to your calendar</a>, or leave your
            email with Professor Oak and he'll write when it's out.
          </p>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* A question wraps onto a second line of its plank when it must (the plank is another component's, hence global). */
  .faq :global(dt) {
    white-space: normal;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .faq dd {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 36rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgb(248 248 248 / 0.8);
  }

  .faq dd ul {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: square;
  }

  .faq dd strong {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .faq dd a {
    color: var(--color-sign);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    text-decoration-color: rgb(230 172 123 / 0.45);
  }

  .faq dd a:hover {
    color: var(--color-sign-light);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }
</style>
